Written: one row, `ai-regulation`, chair **3**.

- **Passage** (`165e3a2a…`): AB 316 (2025-2026), authored by Krell ("AB 316, Krell."), chaptered 2025-10-13 — `own-act` / `on-question` / `record` (`author`) / `chair-shaped` / `in-term`. No `tally_quote`: the group is `author`, not `vote`.
- **Chair 3** — "Hold AI developers legally responsible when their systems cause harm." The bill's whole operative section bars the autonomy defense in harm actions against anyone who "developed, modified, or used artificial intelligence." Single-subject civil-liability act, so the omnibus problem doesn't arise; it imposes no safety testing (rung 4) or pre-deployment approval (rung 5), and as binding law it isn't voluntary guidelines (rung 2) or non-interference (rung 1).
- **`needs_source`**: her own words answering this question, to test whether she also backs pre-deployment testing — the record here evidences the liability rung only.
- No quotes: the only source is statutory text, not her words.
